  "result": "Unit mismatch. JWT `exp` is **seconds** since epoch. `Date.now()` returns **milliseconds**.\n\nSo `Date.now() > token.exp` compares ~1.7 trillion to ~1.7 billion \u2014 expired tokens always pass.\n\n**Broken:**\n```js\nif (Date.now() > decoded.exp) {\n  return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Token expired' });\n}\n```\n\n**Fixed:**\n```js\nif (Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) > decoded.exp) {\n  return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Token expired' });\n}\n```\n\nOr equivalently:\n```js\nif (Date.now() > decoded.exp * 1000) {\n  return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Token expired' });\n}\n```\n\nSide note: if using `jsonwebtoken` library, pass `{ ignoreExpiration: false }` (default) to `jwt.verify()` and let it handle expiry \u2014 avoids rolling this manually.",
